# Who must approve changes to which paths (SOP-SDLC-001, GitHub Workflow Guide section 3).
#
# People:
#   @GamitPrince       repository owner, project manager, firmware developer, gateway developer
#   @ArkinGamit        dashboard developer
#   @SHINE-18          dashboard developer
#   @gamitriyan-del    electrical engineer (EE)
# Every person listed must be a collaborator with write access, or the rule is ignored.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, and the ruleset requires code-owner approval.
# An author cannot approve their own pull request, so every path below has at least
# two owners, or an owner who is not the usual author. General folders (firmware/,
# gateway/, dashboard/ ...) are not listed: they rely on the ruleset's rule of one
# independent approval from anyone with write access.

# Safety functions: only the EE can approve (Workflow Guide rule 6). Because the EE
# cannot approve their own pull request, a second owner must be added here before the
# EE ever edits these folders (for example a second electrical engineer).
/firmware/src/safety/   @gamitriyan-del
/docs/safety/           @gamitriyan-del

# Register map and API contract: any one of these satisfies this rule, and the
# "interfaces-review" check then requires all three people (the author counts as one).
/interfaces/            @GamitPrince @ArkinGamit @SHINE-18

# CI, repository policy and scripts: stops a feature pull request from quietly
# weakening a check or the 80% coverage gate. Any one of the three developers who is
# not the author can approve.
/.github/               @GamitPrince @ArkinGamit @SHINE-18
/scripts/               @GamitPrince @ArkinGamit @SHINE-18
